1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,681
California,

2
00:00:01,681 --> 00:00:03,580
eighteen forty-nine.

3
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:04,740
Gold!

4
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:07,132
Crowds of dreamers rush into the hills

5
00:00:07,132 --> 00:00:08,530
with their pans.

6
00:00:08,630 --> 00:00:10,580
Most of them find mud.

7
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:11,078
But down in town,

8
00:00:11,078 --> 00:00:11,724
one storekeeper is having the best year

9
00:00:11,724 --> 00:00:12,270
of her life.

10
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:15,860
She doesn't dig.

11
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:17,200
She sells the shovels.

12
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,454
Today there's a new gold rush,

13
00:00:19,454 --> 00:00:21,110
and it's called AI.

14
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:24,791
Everyone is watching the companies that

15
00:00:24,791 --> 00:00:26,730
build the chatbots.

16
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,635
But some countries are getting rich the

17
00:00:28,635 --> 00:00:29,240
old way,

18
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:31,090
by selling the shovels.

19
00:00:31,250 --> 00:00:33,230
So which countries could win the AI

20
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:36,553
economy without building AI at all?

21
00:00:47,417 --> 00:00:50,229
That storekeeper is make-believe,

22
00:00:50,229 --> 00:00:52,377
but the pattern is real.

23
00:00:52,477 --> 00:00:53,998
In the actual Gold Rush,

24
00:00:53,998 --> 00:00:56,423
a merchant named Sam Brannan became known

25
00:00:56,423 --> 00:00:59,227
as the richest man in California.

26
00:00:59,427 --> 00:01:01,317
He never mined for gold.

27
00:01:01,387 --> 00:01:03,345
His stores sold the miners what they

28
00:01:03,345 --> 00:01:03,976
needed,

29
00:01:03,976 --> 00:01:06,534
at whatever price the rush would pay.

30
00:01:06,783 --> 00:01:08,473
Meet Hattie.

31
00:01:08,633 --> 00:01:10,875
Her family has run the same hardware

32
00:01:10,875 --> 00:01:13,319
store in gold country for generations,

33
00:01:13,319 --> 00:01:15,336
and the old rule is still painted

34
00:01:15,336 --> 00:01:16,833
above the door.

35
00:01:17,163 --> 00:01:18,248
In a rush,

36
00:01:18,248 --> 00:01:19,683
sell shovels.

37
00:01:19,993 --> 00:01:21,411
One sleepy morning,

38
00:01:21,411 --> 00:01:23,933
a package lands on her counter.

39
00:01:24,223 --> 00:01:26,490
Inside is a tiny AI chip,

40
00:01:26,490 --> 00:01:28,873
the kind that runs a chatbot.

41
00:01:29,093 --> 00:01:30,423
And it talks.

42
00:01:30,583 --> 00:01:31,109
Hi,

43
00:01:31,109 --> 00:01:32,163
it says.

44
00:01:32,163 --> 00:01:33,313
I'm Nugget.

45
00:01:33,313 --> 00:01:35,059
I've been everywhere.

46
00:01:35,317 --> 00:01:37,184
Nugget has a passport,

47
00:01:37,184 --> 00:01:39,327
and it's packed with stamps.

48
00:01:39,327 --> 00:01:41,107
Hattie flips through it.

49
00:01:41,257 --> 00:01:43,199
This little chip was printed on an

50
00:01:43,199 --> 00:01:43,824
island,

51
00:01:43,824 --> 00:01:45,550
with a machine from a flat green

52
00:01:45,550 --> 00:01:46,175
country,

53
00:01:46,175 --> 00:01:48,717
and memory from across the sea.

54
00:01:48,847 --> 00:01:50,608
Its tools and chemicals came from

55
00:01:50,608 --> 00:01:52,127
somewhere else again,

56
00:01:52,127 --> 00:01:53,866
its money from the desert,

57
00:01:53,866 --> 00:01:56,227
and its metal from the mountains.

58
00:01:56,357 --> 00:01:58,987
Every stamp is a shovel shop.

59
00:01:58,987 --> 00:02:00,777
Hattie grabs her hat.

60
00:02:00,777 --> 00:02:03,125
Let's go meet the shopkeepers.

61
00:02:03,383 --> 00:02:05,985
Let me draw why the shovel sellers

62
00:02:05,985 --> 00:02:07,163
matter.

63
00:02:07,523 --> 00:02:08,196
At the top,

64
00:02:08,196 --> 00:02:09,578
someone builds a chatbot and sells

65
00:02:09,578 --> 00:02:10,263
answers.

66
00:02:10,263 --> 00:02:11,590
To do that,

67
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:14,563
they rent a data center.

68
00:02:14,563 --> 00:02:16,793
The data center buys chips.

69
00:02:16,793 --> 00:02:18,714
The chip factory buys machines,

70
00:02:18,714 --> 00:02:20,593
memory and chemicals.

71
00:02:20,593 --> 00:02:22,277
And all of it needs power,

72
00:02:22,277 --> 00:02:23,943
money and metal.

73
00:02:24,083 --> 00:02:26,658
Every dollar spent at the top rolls

74
00:02:26,658 --> 00:02:27,405
downhill,

75
00:02:27,405 --> 00:02:29,293
through the shovel shops.

76
00:02:29,643 --> 00:02:31,053
And here's the trick.

77
00:02:31,143 --> 00:02:32,683
The shops at the top have rivals

78
00:02:32,683 --> 00:02:34,053
everywhere.

79
00:02:34,243 --> 00:02:36,558
Some shops near the bottom have almost

80
00:02:36,558 --> 00:02:37,415
none.

81
00:02:41,850 --> 00:02:42,898
First stamp,

82
00:02:42,898 --> 00:02:44,220
Taiwan.

83
00:02:44,350 --> 00:02:45,582
Nugget was born here,

84
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:48,480
in a chip factory called a foundry.

85
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:50,729
Its design came from America,

86
00:02:50,729 --> 00:02:52,900
but almost nobody else on Earth can

87
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:55,020
actually build it this small.

88
00:02:55,290 --> 00:02:57,810
Hattie watches the line outside.

89
00:02:57,810 --> 00:02:59,405
The biggest names in tech,

90
00:02:59,405 --> 00:03:01,560
all waiting at the same counter.

91
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:02,545
Excuse me,

92
00:03:02,545 --> 00:03:03,510
she asks.

93
00:03:03,510 --> 00:03:05,300
Is this the only shop?

94
00:03:05,510 --> 00:03:06,461
Pretty much,

95
00:03:06,461 --> 00:03:07,793
says Nugget.

96
00:03:08,050 --> 00:03:09,900
The shop is called TSMC.

97
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:10,781
Last year,

98
00:03:10,781 --> 00:03:13,818
it sold about a hundred and twenty

99
00:03:13,818 --> 00:03:15,914
billion dollars of chips,

100
00:03:15,914 --> 00:03:18,640
the most in its history.

101
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:21,255
And every new AI model needs more

102
00:03:21,255 --> 00:03:22,342
of them.

103
00:03:22,583 --> 00:03:24,853
The whole island feels it.

104
00:03:25,063 --> 00:03:27,685
Taiwan's exports smashed their record,

105
00:03:27,685 --> 00:03:30,069
and for the first time in twenty-six

106
00:03:30,069 --> 00:03:30,572
years,

107
00:03:30,572 --> 00:03:34,254
America became Taiwan's biggest customer,

108
00:03:34,254 --> 00:03:36,973
ahead of China and Hong Kong.

109
00:03:37,053 --> 00:03:38,743
Its biggest shipments?

110
00:03:38,743 --> 00:03:42,106
Servers and chips for the AI rush.

111
00:03:42,350 --> 00:03:44,586
The government's statistics office now

112
00:03:44,586 --> 00:03:47,269
forecasts that Taiwan's economy will grow

113
00:03:47,269 --> 00:03:49,281
faster this year than at any time

114
00:03:49,281 --> 00:03:51,670
since nineteen eighty-seven.

115
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:53,210
Hattie stares.

116
00:03:53,210 --> 00:03:53,998
All that,

117
00:03:53,998 --> 00:03:55,956
from selling shovels?

118
00:03:56,217 --> 00:03:58,690
Being the only shop in town is

119
00:03:58,690 --> 00:04:00,217
powerful.

120
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:02,490
It's also a little nerve-racking,

121
00:04:02,490 --> 00:04:04,784
for the island and for every customer

122
00:04:04,784 --> 00:04:05,957
in the line.

123
00:04:06,287 --> 00:04:08,293
We told that story in The Small

124
00:04:08,293 --> 00:04:12,154
Island the Whole World Economy Depends On.

125
00:04:12,417 --> 00:04:13,543
Second stamp,

126
00:04:13,543 --> 00:04:15,167
the Netherlands.

127
00:04:15,167 --> 00:04:15,991
A flat,

128
00:04:15,991 --> 00:04:19,717
green country with one very unusual shop.

129
00:04:19,867 --> 00:04:22,075
Nugget's tiniest lines were printed with

130
00:04:22,075 --> 00:04:22,495
light,

131
00:04:22,495 --> 00:04:24,924
by a machine that only one company

132
00:04:24,924 --> 00:04:26,006
on Earth can build,

133
00:04:26,006 --> 00:04:26,717
ASML.

134
00:04:26,717 --> 00:04:29,184
Each machine is about the size of

135
00:04:29,184 --> 00:04:29,979
a bus,

136
00:04:29,979 --> 00:04:32,145
and it travels in pieces,

137
00:04:32,145 --> 00:04:34,938
packed into cargo planes.

138
00:04:35,183 --> 00:04:37,662
One of these machines costs about two

139
00:04:37,662 --> 00:04:40,493
hundred and fifty million dollars.

140
00:04:40,503 --> 00:04:42,593
And if you want the most advanced

141
00:04:42,593 --> 00:04:43,035
chips,

142
00:04:43,035 --> 00:04:45,493
there is no second shop to try.

143
00:04:45,733 --> 00:04:47,173
Hattie whispers.

144
00:04:47,173 --> 00:04:49,039
Now that's a shovel.

145
00:04:49,283 --> 00:04:51,944
But even the only shop doesn't get

146
00:04:51,944 --> 00:04:54,613
to choose all its customers.

147
00:04:54,703 --> 00:04:57,221
Governments decide where these machines

148
00:04:57,221 --> 00:04:57,951
may go,

149
00:04:57,951 --> 00:04:59,688
and ASML's biggest market,

150
00:04:59,688 --> 00:05:00,418
China,

151
00:05:00,418 --> 00:05:03,439
has never been allowed the most advanced

152
00:05:03,439 --> 00:05:04,543
ones.

153
00:05:04,803 --> 00:05:06,760
We took the machine apart in The

154
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:09,970
Machine Every Advanced Chip Depends On.

155
00:05:14,417 --> 00:05:15,484
Third stamp,

156
00:05:15,484 --> 00:05:17,187
South Korea.

157
00:05:17,267 --> 00:05:18,894
Nugget's brain is fast,

158
00:05:18,894 --> 00:05:20,597
but forgetful.

159
00:05:20,617 --> 00:05:23,244
It needs a special memory stacked right

160
00:05:23,244 --> 00:05:24,175
beside it,

161
00:05:24,175 --> 00:05:25,107
layer on layer,

162
00:05:25,107 --> 00:05:27,467
like a tower of pancakes.

163
00:05:27,467 --> 00:05:29,447
It's called HBM.

164
00:05:29,447 --> 00:05:32,105
Only a handful of companies can make

165
00:05:32,105 --> 00:05:32,564
it,

166
00:05:32,564 --> 00:05:35,097
and the leader is SK hynix.

167
00:05:35,227 --> 00:05:36,210
I'm hungry,

168
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:37,507
says Nugget.

169
00:05:37,507 --> 00:05:38,780
You're a chip,

170
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:40,033
says Hattie.

171
00:05:40,283 --> 00:05:42,313
Let me draw what the AI rush

172
00:05:42,313 --> 00:05:44,943
