173
00:05:45,283 --> 00:05:45,613
Not long ago,

174
00:05:45,613 --> 00:05:46,483
SK hynix was losing money.

175
00:05:46,483 --> 00:05:48,783
Memory prices had crashed.

176
00:05:48,783 --> 00:05:50,883
Then the rush arrived.

177
00:05:50,883 --> 00:05:52,285
The next year,

178
00:05:52,285 --> 00:05:53,593
a record.

179
00:05:53,593 --> 00:05:54,985
The year after that,

180
00:05:54,985 --> 00:05:57,580
its operating profit roughly doubled

181
00:05:57,580 --> 00:05:58,264
again,

182
00:05:58,264 --> 00:06:01,163
to about thirty-three billion dollars.

183
00:06:01,163 --> 00:06:02,265
For the first time,

184
00:06:02,265 --> 00:06:04,665
it out-earned all of Samsung.

185
00:06:04,917 --> 00:06:08,017
And the whole country rode along.

186
00:06:08,057 --> 00:06:10,239
South Korea's chip exports set a new

187
00:06:10,239 --> 00:06:13,147
record of about a hundred and seventy

188
00:06:13,147 --> 00:06:14,717
billion dollars.

189
00:06:15,037 --> 00:06:16,987
Hattie whistles.

190
00:06:17,107 --> 00:06:19,499
That's a lot of pancakes.

191
00:06:19,750 --> 00:06:20,253
Fourth stamp,

192
00:06:20,253 --> 00:06:21,020
Japan.

193
00:06:21,020 --> 00:06:22,240
No famous chatbot here either.

194
00:06:22,450 --> 00:06:24,980
But look closer.

195
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:27,203
The machines that coat,

196
00:06:27,203 --> 00:06:29,186
etch and clean each wafer,

197
00:06:29,186 --> 00:06:32,660
from companies like Tokyo Electron.

198
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:34,637
The ultra-pure chemicals and the

199
00:06:34,637 --> 00:06:36,376
light-sensitive coatings that chip

200
00:06:36,376 --> 00:06:39,150
factories everywhere depend on.

201
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:42,463
Japanese companies make most of them.

202
00:06:42,717 --> 00:06:45,095
Japan's shovel shops rarely make

203
00:06:45,095 --> 00:06:46,487
headlines.

204
00:06:46,487 --> 00:06:49,297
They make the parts nobody can skip.

205
00:06:49,437 --> 00:06:49,856
Quiet,

206
00:06:49,856 --> 00:06:50,495
steady,

207
00:06:50,495 --> 00:06:52,637
and very hard to copy.

208
00:06:52,927 --> 00:06:56,198
We opened that cabinet in The Chemicals

209
00:06:56,198 --> 00:06:59,217
Nobody Talks About That Decide Who Makes

210
00:06:59,217 --> 00:06:59,695
Chips,

211
00:06:59,695 --> 00:07:01,960
and Japan's robot bet in Will AI

212
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:04,069
Make Japan Rich Again?

213
00:07:08,517 --> 00:07:09,701
Fifth stamp,

214
00:07:09,701 --> 00:07:11,117
the Gulf.

215
00:07:11,297 --> 00:07:13,557
Here the shovel isn't a machine.

216
00:07:13,557 --> 00:07:14,670
It's money,

217
00:07:14,670 --> 00:07:16,127
and sunshine.

218
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:17,181
Funds built on oil money are now

219
00:07:17,181 --> 00:07:18,267
