00:09:49,323 --> 00:09:50,623
Let me draw it.

294
00:09:50,623 --> 00:09:51,671
On one side,

295
00:09:51,671 --> 00:09:54,153
the shovels anyone can sell.

296
00:09:54,183 --> 00:09:54,912
Metal,

297
00:09:54,912 --> 00:09:55,640
money,

298
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:56,653
power.

299
00:09:56,653 --> 00:09:59,035
Their price rises and falls with the

300
00:09:59,035 --> 00:09:59,933
rush.

301
00:10:00,033 --> 00:10:01,241
On the other side,

302
00:10:01,241 --> 00:10:03,683
the shovels nobody else can make.

303
00:10:03,693 --> 00:10:04,577
The foundry,

304
00:10:04,577 --> 00:10:05,460
the machine,

305
00:10:05,460 --> 00:10:07,873
the most advanced memory.

306
00:10:07,963 --> 00:10:09,888
Those shops get to set their own

307
00:10:09,888 --> 00:10:10,763
price.

308
00:10:10,943 --> 00:10:13,563
The safest shovel isn't the biggest one.

309
00:10:13,563 --> 00:10:16,102
It's the one with no second shop.

310
00:10:16,350 --> 00:10:18,840
Hattie writes up her scorecard.

311
00:10:19,190 --> 00:10:21,108
Taiwan and the Netherlands,

312
00:10:21,108 --> 00:10:21,812
winning,

313
00:10:21,812 --> 00:10:24,240
as long as nobody builds a second

314
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:26,540
shop and politics stays calm.

315
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:27,889
South Korea,

316
00:10:27,889 --> 00:10:28,878
winning big,

317
00:10:28,878 --> 00:10:31,000
on a rollercoaster.

318
00:10:31,260 --> 00:10:32,153
Japan,

319
00:10:32,153 --> 00:10:34,910
steady and hard to replace.

320
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:35,850
The Gulf,

321
00:10:35,850 --> 00:10:38,590
buying a seat at every table.

322
00:10:38,770 --> 00:10:40,345
Chile and Australia,

323
00:10:40,345 --> 00:10:41,691
rich in the good years,

324
00:10:41,691 --> 00:10:44,117
exposed in the bad ones.

325
00:10:44,383 --> 00:10:46,468
So can a country win the AI

326
00:10:46,468 --> 00:10:49,413
economy without building AI?

327
00:10:49,563 --> 00:10:50,423
Yes.

328
00:10:50,423 --> 00:10:52,103
Some already are.

329
00:10:52,183 --> 00:10:54,014
But the winners aren't the ones who

330
00:10:54,014 --> 00:10:55,163
dig the most.

331
00:10:55,273 --> 00:10:57,232
They're the ones who own a shovel

332
00:10:57,232 --> 00:10:58,733
nobody can copy,

333
00:10:58,733 --> 00:11:00,909
and keep inventing the next one before

334
00:11:00,909 --> 00:11:02,598
the rush moves on.

335
00:11:02,850 --> 00:11:03,732
Back home,

336
00:11:03,732 --> 00:11:06,970
Hattie repaints the sign above her door.

337
00:11:06,970 --> 00:11:09,000
Nugget hops onto the counter.

338
00:11:09,030 --> 00:11:10,740
So what do we sell now?

339
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:12,420
Hattie smiles.

340
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:15,325
Whatever they can't get anywhere else.

341
00:11:15,583 --> 00:11:16,203
Next time,

342
00:11:16,203 --> 00:11:18,983
we follow the money behind another hidden

343
00:11:18,983 --> 00:11:21,293
link of the world economy.

344
00:11:21,393 --> 00:11:23,472
This is The Hidden Economics.
